%description:

TcpCubic.hystartLowWindow:other -- HyStart ends slow start only at a window of 400 segments or more.

The claim (TcpCubic.ned): "smallest cwnd (in segments) at which HyStart starts looking for the
exit point".

The classes: linux (16, the default, the value of Linux tcp_cubic.c), other (a larger
value), invalid (below 0). The code: HyStart acts in slow start when the window is at least hystartLowWindow segments
(TcpCubic::processRttSample()). TcpCubic::hystartUpdate() looks for the exit: detector 1, the
ACK train, and detector 2, the delay increase, whose threshold is the minimum RTT / 8, clamped
to hystartDelayMin and hystartDelayMax (TcpCubic::hystartDelayThresh()). At the exit, ssthresh
becomes the window. TcpCubic::initializeAlgorithm() checks the values. This test separates "other" from "linux": the queue grows before the window has 400
segments.

Host under test: host1, with TcpCubic and HyStart, which sends to host2; the path is host1 -- tap -- router -- host2, with a bottleneck of 10 Mbps from the router to
host2 and a round trip of 40 ms. host2 has a window of 1000000 bytes and acknowledges each
second segment (the delayed ACK), so its ACKs come 2.4 ms apart, more than the ACK delta of 2
ms: they form no ACK train, and only the queue at the bottleneck can end slow start. Observation: level 3, at 1.2 s, HyStart found the exit, and the threshold, the window at
the exit, is at least 400 segments of 1448 bytes, 579200 bytes.

%# parameter: TcpCubic.hystartLowWindow
%# class: other
%# value: 400
%# key: *.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.hystartLowWindow
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpCubicHystartLowWindowOther")
        .act(action().at(1.2)
                 .describe("the state at 1.2 s")
                 .assertModule("host1.tcp.conn-*", "state.hystart_found == true && state.ssthresh >= 579200"));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpCubicHystartLowWindowOther compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.hystartLowWindow = 400    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpCubic"
network = inet.protocoltest.TapRouterNetwork
*.linkDelay = 5ms
*.bottleneckDatarate = 10Mbps
*.bottleneckDelay = 10ms
*.host2.tcp.advertisedWindow = 1000000
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 10000000B
sim-time-limit = 1.3s
*.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.hystartEnabled = true
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpCubicHystartLowWindowOther: PASS
